\fs28 	\'85ops resources contain info on planetary disasters. Actually, the term \'d2disasters\'d3 is a misnomer, as these occurances simply affect the price of a single commodity at a planet or station, for good or bad. Override uses the name of the resource in the commodity exchange dialog box to indicate that a disaster is currently going on at a planet. The fields of an \'9aops resource are:\
\
Stellar		The stellar object this disaster is linked to\
	\cf2 128-1628	ID of a stellar object\
\cf0 	-1		Any planet or station (use sparingly)\
	\cf2 -2		Nothing (used for mission-related news)\cf0 \
\
Commodity \
Which commodity to affect the price of (0 = food, 1 = industrial, etc...)\
\
\cf2 PriceDelta	How much to raise or lower the price. (negative numbers lower it)\cf0 \
\
Duration	How many days the disaster lasts.\
\
\cf2 Freq		Percent chance per day that the disaster will occur.\cf0 \
\
MissionBit	Tells Override how to relate mission bits and disasters. (see m\'95sn for more info)\
	\cf2 -1		Ignored\cf0 \
	0-511		Activate the disaster when this mission bit is set\
	\cf2 1000-1511	Don\'d5t allow this disaster to occur unless this mission bit is set\
\cf0 	2000-2511	Allow this disaster to occur only if this mission bit is cleared\
	\cf2 3000-3511	Activate the disaster when this mission bit is cleared}